      "extract": "E-mail: meliot@phare.normalesup.org Abstract In this paper, we review the representation theory of the inﬁnite symmetric group, and we extend the works of Kerov and Vershik by proving that the irreducible characters of S∞always satisfy a central limit theorem. Hence, for any point of the Thoma simplex, the corresponding measures on the levels Yn of the Young graph have a property of gaussian concentration. By using",
